## Account profile

- **Segment:** Enterprise.
- **Size:** 200 seats across 3 BUs (Operations, Finance, RevOps).
- **Contract:** $180k ARR, annual prepay, started 2025-09-30. Renews 2026-09-30.
- **Plan:** Enterprise tier with custom SLA on export latency (<5s p95).
- **Expansion path:** Per-seat add-on for the 60 unlicensed users in Finance BU. Gated on per-seat invoicing landing.

## Usage shape

- DAU/MAU = 0.62 (was 0.71 in Q1; declining).
- Export feature usage dropped 18% MoM after we shipped the new rate limits in 2026-04. Likely correlation, not causation — confirm before next QBR.
- Activation event triggered on 187 of 200 seats; 13 inactive users concentrated in Finance BU (the same BU as the expansion candidate seats).
- Top 5 export queries account for 80% of traffic; one of them is the failing query for SLA misses.

## Health signals

- 2 support tickets in May 2026 about export latency; one breached the SLA.
- NPS shifted from +40 (Q1) to +20 (Q2) — sample of 8 responses.
- Two recent renewals at this account tier (Globalcorp, Northwind) cited export latency as the primary deal-breaker; Acme has not made the same complaint *yet* but the trajectory matches.
- No support tickets about billing; Finance team uses an external billing-reconciliation tool to work around the per-seat-invoice gap.
- 2026-05-20 — Export SLA breach reported on 2026-05-19 (second breach in 30 days).

## Decision drivers

- **Strong yes on:** export latency improvements, per-seat invoicing for >100-seat accounts, SLA-credit auto-application.
- **Strong no on:** UX changes that retrain admin workflows (Acme is conservative on UI shifts).
- **Neutral but vocal:** mobile experience (asked about it twice but never blocked on it).

## Stakeholders

- **Hugo** (Head of Operations, 32 of their seats) — see `2026-05-19-hugo-acme-ops` for his open asks. Primary day-to-day contact.
- **Devlin** (CFO; not yet captured in chronicle) — owner of the per-seat invoicing ask. Worth opening a stakeholder entry next time we hear from him.

## Notes

The export-latency hypothesis (`2026-05-18-export-latency-drives-enterprise-churn`) is being tested against this account specifically. Acme is on the watch-list for falsifier triggers — if their renewal lands without an export fix, the hypothesis weakens; if it doesn't, it strengthens.
